<title>USA: Santa Fe ups stake in Kazakhstan project.</title>
<headline>Santa Fe ups stake in Kazakhstan project.</headline>
<dateline>ALBUQUERQUE, N.M. 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santa Fe Pacific Gold Corp Wednesday said it increased its interest in the Sharaltyn exploration project to 100 percent from 50 percent at a price of $3.05 million.</p>
<p>The project covers a 7.5 million-acre license area in northeastern Kazakhstan.  The 50 percent carried interest in the project is currently held by two state-owned entities, the company said.</p>
<p>The transaction will become final within three to four weeks after registration with the Republic of Kazakhstan's Ministry of Justice, Santa Fe said.</p>
